Longlist,70,B,Safety,,Singapore University of Technology and Design,BEng (Engineering Product Development) — Healthcare Engineering Design track,Singapore,Singapore (Changi/Upper Changi),"Not ranked in QS Engineering & Technology top tiers (young, small, design-led institution)",Not in QS world top 100,A-Level with Mathematics + Physics/Chemistry; SUTD admissions are holistic (portfolio/interview element). Capped international quota.,A*A*A*A (predicted),Yes,IELTS/TOEFL required for international applicants (exact minimum to confirm),,"SGD 19000 (ESTIMATE — Tier C subsidised rate is NOT published; ASEAN non-subsidised is SGD 30,200/yr AY2026)",SGD 76000,SGD 13000,4,"448,000.00",SUTD undergraduate scholarships — sutd.edu.sg/admissions/undergraduate. No ASEAN auto-consideration equivalent to NUS/NTU.,,,,,"MOE Tuition Grant bond = 3 years at a Singapore-registered company after graduation — IF the (competitive, limited) Tier C grant is awarded","EAB-ACCREDITED (IES Engineering Accreditation Board) — BEng (Engineering Product Development) fully accredited for students graduating in/after AY2014/2015. Washington Accord -> BEM (Ir.) path. NOTE: accredited as EPD, not as Biomedical Engineering. Verified on the official ies.org.sg EAB list (as of Dec 2025). MQA: verify.",SUTD undergraduate admissions online application,2027-02-28 (EST. — confirm exact AY2027/28 international dates),2027 Aug/Sept,"The realistic third Singapore option, and his most likely SG admit — but a clear step down on the two things he weights most (ranking 0.20 + scholarship 0.20). COURSE CAVEAT: biomedical is a SPECIALISATION TRACK inside a general Engineering Product Development degree — he would graduate an EPD engineer with a healthcare focus, NOT a biomedical engineer. Track content is genuinely relevant (surgical tools/robots, biomedical instrumentation, biomechanics, imaging, implants, tissue engineering). RECOGNITION IS FINE: BEng EPD is EAB-accredited -> Washington Accord -> BEM. TWO MONEY RISKS: (1) SUTD's Tier C subsidised rate is not published anywhere on its fees page — the SGD 19,000 here is an ESTIMATE aligned to NUS/NTU (SGD 18,050) and MUST be verified at Stage 4; the published ASEAN NON-subsidised rate is SGD 30,200/yr. (2) SUTD states explicitly that international Tuition Grants are LIMITED IN NUMBER and awarded competitively on merit — so both the subsidy and the bond pathway are less certain here than at NUS/NTU. Upside: SUTD's entire pedagogy is project/design-based (hence experiential_fit 5).",https://www.sutd.edu.sg/epd/education/undergraduate/specialisation-tracks/healthcare-engineering-design/,Not verified
