Longlist,56,B,Safety,Over budget,Nottingham Trent University,Biomedical Engineering BEng,UK,Nottingham,IET-accredited biomedical engineering; teaching-focused,Not in QS top 500,~BBC-BCC (A-level),A*A*A*A (predicted),Yes,IELTS 6.0-6.5,,"GBP 18700 (approx; NTU international UG range GBP 17,950-18,700)",GBP 56100,GBP 11000,3,"525,690.00",NTU international scholarships/bursaries (partial). ntu.ac.uk/international/fees-scholarships-and-money-matters,,,,,"UK Graduate Route (18 months for 2027 applicants), then Skilled Worker visa",BEng ACCREDITED by the IET (Engineering Council); UK = Washington Accord. MQA: verify; confirm BEM registrability (biomedical).,UCAS,2027-01-14 (UCAS equal consideration),2027 Sept,Cheapest of the set and IET-accredited. Course URL is the fees page — confirm the exact biomedical-eng course link at Stage 4. Clear Safety / strong value hedge for his scholarship gate. English test not yet sat.,https://www.ntu.ac.uk/international/tuition-fees,Not verified
Longlist,49,C,Safety,,University of Cyberjaya (UoC),Bachelor of Biomedical Engineering Technology (Honours),Malaysia,"Cyberjaya, Selangor",Not ranked,Not ranked,"A-Level / STPM / Foundation, low bar. He is far above it.",A*A*A*A (predicted),Yes,Modest; confirm,,MYR 21000 (ESTIMATE; verify),MYR 84000 (ESTIMATE),MYR 18000,4,"156,000.00",Affordable without a scholarship; UoC merit awards exist. cyberjaya.edu.my,,,,n/a - Malaysian citizen,n/a - home country. NO migration pathway.,"WRONG LADDER FOR HIM. Accredited by the ENGINEERING TECHNOLOGY Accreditation Council (ETAC) under BEM, recognised by the SYDNEY Accord -> leads to MBOT Professional Technologist (Ts.), NOT BEM Professional Engineer (Ir.), NOT the Washington Accord. His profile.recognition_targets names BEM + Washington Accord -> this FAILS his own gate.",Direct to University of Cyberjaya,2027-08-31 (ESTIMATE; verify),2027 (Feb / Sept),"KEPT DELIBERATELY AS A NEGATIVE FINDING - the Malaysian mirror of SUSS in Singapore. The title reads 'Biomedical Engineering' and looks like a perfect course match, but the degree is 'Biomedical Engineering TECHNOLOGY' and UoC's own material confirms ETAC accreditation + Sydney Accord recognition. That is the Ts. (MBOT) ladder, not the Ir. (BEM) ladder he asked for, and the two are NOT interchangeable for a regulated profession. Corroborating evidence: UoC is ABSENT from the EAC accredited-institution list (checked 2026-07-16). Recommend formal Rejected at Stage 4 with this reasoning. Same trap, same category: UniKL BMI's 'Bachelor of Electronic Engineering Technology (Medical Electronics)' is ETAC too (etac.org.my, Mar 2025) - if he asks about it, the answer is identical. Scored honestly rather than dropped so he can see WHY it fails.",https://cyberjaya.edu.my/programme/bachelor-of-biomedical-engineering-technology-hons,Not verified
Longlist,29,C,,,Singapore University of Social Sciences,BSc Biomedical Engineering,Singapore,Singapore (Clementi),Not ranked,Not ranked,Part-time programme aimed at working adults; A-Level H2 Maths grade D or better satisfies the maths prerequisite. NOT open to international students on a Student's Pass.,A*A*A*A (predicted),,,,,,,4,,,,,,,None — part-time study confers no Student's Pass and no MOE Tuition Grant bond pathway,NOT EAB-accredited. SUSS's only EAB-accredited engineering degrees are BEng (Aerospace Systems) and BEng (Electronics Engineering) — the BSc Biomedical Engineering is NOT on the IES EAB list (checked Dec 2025 list). It confers IES STUDENT MEMBERSHIP only. FAILS his BEM / Washington Accord recognition target.,SUSS online application,"2026-09-30 (application window 1 Apr - 30 Sep 2026, for a JANUARY 2027 intake)",2027 Jan (part-time),"NEGATIVE FINDING — kept on the list deliberately so it is not 're-discovered' as a match later. This is the ONLY other degree in Singapore literally titled 'Biomedical Engineering', so it looks like a perfect course_match on the title alone. It is not viable, on two independent counts: (1) LADDER: it is a Bachelor of SCIENCE, not a Bachelor of ENGINEERING, and it is absent from the IES EAB accredited-programme list — so it does NOT carry Washington Accord recognition and does NOT lead to BEM (Ir.) registration. His profile.recognition_targets names BEM + Washington Accord, so this fails his own stated gate even though the title matches exactly — the exact trap workflows/03 warns about. It offers IES student membership only, which is not accreditation. (2) MODE: it is a PART-TIME programme for working adults with a January intake; international students cannot obtain a Student's Pass for part-time study, so he could not enrol from Malaysia at all. Fees left blank because no international full-time fee exists. Recommend formal Rejected at Stage 4 with this reasoning recorded.",https://www.suss.edu.sg/programmes/detail/bsc-biomedical-engineering,Not verified
shortlist,97,A,Match,,Nanyang Technological University,BEng (Bioengineering),Singapore,Singapore (Jurong West),"QS Engineering & Technology #10 world (2026), #2 Asia",QS #12 world (2026),International students: Mathematics at senior high school level + Physics/Chemistry/Biology at senior high school level. (A-Level equivalent: H2 Maths + H2 Physics/Chem/Bio.) Selection is competitive + capped international quota.,A*A*A*A (predicted),Yes,IELTS/TOEFL required for international applicants (exact minimum to confirm),Accelerated Bachelor's Programme (ABP) — finish in 3.5 yrs if eligible,"SGD 18050 (ASEAN international WITH MOE Tuition Grant, lab-based; SGD 40,600 without)",SGD 72200,SGD 13000,4,"434,700.00",NTU ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship — considered via the admission application. ntu.edu.sg/admissions/undergraduate/scholarships,Full subsidised tuition + living/accommodation allowances (NTU ASEAN UG Scholarship — mirrors the NUS structure; confirm exact quantum at Stage 4).,,,,"MOE Tuition Grant bond = must work for a Singapore-registered company for 3 years immediately after graduation — a guaranteed graduate work pathway, not a lottery",EAB-ACCREDITED (IES Engineering Accreditation Board) — BEng (Bioengineering) fully accredited for students graduating in/after AY2007/2008. IES is the Singapore Washington Accord signatory -> BEM (Ir.) path. Verified on the official ies.org.sg EAB list (as of Dec 2025). MQA: verify.,NTU Office of Admissions online application,2027-02-15 (EST. — NTU international window typically ~Nov to Feb; confirm exact AY2027/28 dates),"2027 Aug (Singapore AY starts August, not September)","Co-flagship with NUS; near-identical cost/funding/recognition case. TITLE CHECK: the degree is 'Bioengineering', not 'Biomedical Engineering' — but it is the correct Washington Accord ladder (Bachelor of ENGINEERING, EAB-accredited since AY2007/08), NOT the Engineering Technology/ETAC ladder, so it satisfies his BEM target. Curriculum is squarely biomedical: medical device design, biomechanics, bioinstrumentation, regulatory affairs from year 1, hospital attachments. EXPERIENTIAL EDGE OVER NUS: compulsory semester-long internship + URECA undergrad research + Global Immersion Programme (6-month stints incl. USA/Switzerland/France). Fee = SGD 18,050/yr ASEAN-international WITH MOE Tuition Grant (lab-based rate), SGD 40,600 without — from the official NTU AY2026 tuition page. Same caveat as NUS: the TG is quota-limited and carries the 3-yr bond; without it the budget case collapses (~RM700k). Same UNEVIDENCED SCHOLARSHIP RISK as NUS: the ASEAN UG Scholarship weighs leadership + co-curricular record, and his intake captured neither — scholarship_opportunity 5 reflects the funding STRUCTURE, not his odds of winning it. Living cost SGD 13,000/yr = NUS OAM official estimate, applied to NTU as a proxy.",https://www.ntu.edu.sg/spms/admissions/undergrad/detail/bachelor-of-engineering-in-bioengineering,Not verified
Finalist,96,A,Match,,National University of Singapore,BEng (Biomedical Engineering),Singapore,Singapore (Kent Ridge),"QS Engineering & Technology #8 world (2026), #1 Asia",QS ~#8 world (2026),"A-Level: pass in Mathematics or Further Mathematics (course prerequisite). Selection is by Indicative Grade Profile + capped international quota, not by the bare prerequisite.",A*A*A*A (predicted),Yes,IELTS/TOEFL required for international applicants (exact minimum to confirm),,"SGD 18050 (ASEAN international WITH MOE Tuition Grant; SGD 39,700 without)",SGD 72200,SGD 13000,4,"434,700.00","NUS ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship — auto-considered via the admission application, no separate form. nus.edu.sg/oam/scholarships. Also Science & Technology UG Scholarship + NUS International UG Scholarship.","FULL: 100% of subsidised tuition (after MOE Tuition Grant) + SGD 5,800/yr living allowance + SGD 3,000/yr accommodation allowance + SGD 1,750 one-time computer allowance. No scholarship bond (but the required MOE TG carries the 3-yr bond).",,,,"MOE Tuition Grant bond = must work for a Singapore-registered company for 3 years immediately after graduation — a guaranteed graduate work pathway, not a lottery",EAB-ACCREDITED (IES Engineering Accreditation Board) — BEng (Biomedical Engineering) fully accredited for students graduating in/after AY2013/2014. IES is the Singapore Washington Accord signatory -> BEM (Ir.) path. Verified on the official ies.org.sg EAB list (as of Dec 2025). MQA: verify.,NUS Office of Admissions online application (myaces.nus.edu.sg),2027-02-23 (EST. — the AY2026/27 international window was 3 Dec 2025 to 23 Feb 2026; confirm exact AY2027/28 dates),"2027 Aug (Singapore AY starts August, not September)","VERIFIED 2026-07-23 (official sources): tuition SGD 18,050 (ASEAN w/ MOE TG) / SGD 39,700 (no TG) CONFIRMED on NUS registrar UGTuition PDF (Design & Engineering, AY2026/27 new intake, cohort-locked; AY2027/28 figures publish ~Mar 2027). ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship terms (100% subsidised tuition + SGD 5,800/yr living + SGD 3,000/yr accommodation + SGD 1,750 one-time computer; leadership + CCA + outstanding results; auto-considered; interviews Jan-Jul, outcome mid-July; renewal GPA>=3.50) CONFIRMED on nus.edu.sg/oam. Entry: BEng admission, prereq A-Level pass in Maths/Further Maths (has A* both); Engineering IGP band BBB/C-AAA/A, his A*A*A*A at/above 90th percentile -> Match (capped intl quota). English IELTS 6.5 / TOEFL 92, waivable for English-medium A-Levels. EAB-accredited (BME AY2013/14) -> IES/Washington Accord -> BEM. GES 2025 BME gross salary ~SGD 4,504/mo. Dossier built 2026-07-23. THE flagship option for his gate. (a) COST: first rows in his entire list that may come in UNDER RM500k — SGD 18,050/yr is the ASEAN-international rate WITH the MOE Tuition Grant, from the official NUS registrar UGTuition PDF (AY2026/27, March 2026); the non-subsidised rate is SGD 39,700/yr, which would blow the budget. (b) TUITION GRANT IS NOT AUTOMATIC — it is applied for, quota-limited for internationals, and carries a 3-yr Singapore employment bond; the whole cost case collapses to ~RM680k without it. Verify TG availability at Stage 4. (c) SCHOLARSHIP: as a Malaysian he is ASEAN-eligible for the ASEAN Undergraduate Scholarship, auto-considered through the admission application — the single best match to his hard scholarship gate found in any destination so far. Requires taking the MOE TG. Renewal needs GPA >= 3.50. Interviews Jan-Jul, outcome by mid-July. SCHOLARSHIP RISK — UNEVIDENCED: eligibility also demands 'strong leadership qualities and potential' and a 'good co-curricular activities record', and his intake captured NOTHING on either (interest_discovery/work_styles/values are all empty). Grades alone will not win this. scholarship_opportunity is scored 5 for the STRUCTURE (full ride + stipend, ASEAN-eligible, auto-considered, no separate application — the best funding structure in his entire list); the ODDS are a separate question for scholarship_competitiveness at Stage 4, and hinge on a CCA/leadership record we cannot see. (d) BOND = FEATURE: intent_to_migrate is true, so a 3-yr bond at a Singapore company is a guaranteed job abroad — strictly better than US OPT/H-1B lottery or AU 485. (e) RECOGNITION: officially confirmed on the IES EAB accredited list. (f) Fee/accreditation facts came from official pages this session; source_authority stays Aggregator per Stage 3 convention — Stage 4 flips it after full verification. (g) Living cost SGD 13,000/yr = NUS OAM official estimate (SGD 6,000 excl. accommodation + ~SGD 7,000 on-campus housing, range SGD 4,000-10,290).",https://cde.nus.edu.sg/bme/undergraduate/admissions/,Official page
Finalist,82,A,Reach,,Massachusetts Institute of Technology,Bachelor of Science in Biological Engineering (Course 20),USA,"Cambridge, MA",US News BME #4 (grad); dept globally top-tier,QS ~#1,Holistic admissions — no fixed grade cutoff; SAT/ACT + essays + recommendations; ~4% admit. A*A*A*A is strong but far from sufficient alone.,A*A*A*A (predicted),No,TOEFL/IELTS (Duolingo accepted); likely waived for English-medium A-Levels — confirm,,USD 61990 (2025-26 official),USD 247960,USD 27350,4,"1,679,600.00",MIT is need-blind for international undergrads and meets 100% of demonstrated financial need. No merit scholarships — all aid is need-based. sfs.mit.edu,"Full demonstrated need met (need-based, not merit). No loans in packages.",Aid guaranteed IF admitted — but admission is the ~2% intl bottleneck (holistic).,Apply for aid via CSS Profile + MIT application; aid does not affect admission decision (need-blind).,I-20 requires proof of one year's cost after aid,OPT 12 mo + STEM OPT 24 mo = 3 yrs work authorization. Onward migration via H-1B (annual lottery) then employer green-card sponsorship — uncertain vs AU 485.,"VERIFIED (Stage 4): Course 20 (Biological Engineering) is NOT ABET-accredited — MIT does not seek ABET for it — so it carries NO automatic Washington Accord -> BEM (Ir.) Graduate Engineer path. The ABET-accredited biomedical route at MIT is Course 2-A (Mechanical Eng, biomedical/biomechanics concentration) or Course 10B (Chemical-Biological); both -> Washington Accord -> BEM. MQA individual recognition still plausible on MIT standing, but the automatic ladder needs 2-A/10B, not 20.",MIT application (MIT's own portal — NOT Common App),2027-01-04 (Regular Action Fall 2027; EA 2026-11-01),2027 Sept (Fall),"VERIFIED 2026-07-24 (official MIT sources): AID — need-blind for internationals + meets 100% of demonstrated need, no merit aid (sfs.mit.edu). 2025-26: family income <USD200k -> tuition-free; <USD100k -> full ride (housing/dining/fees too). Net cost is INCOME-DEPENDENT, not the sticker: fundable, likely well under RM500k if admitted -> best answer to his scholarship gate of any option. COA 2025-26 sticker USD89,340/yr (tuition 61,990 + housing 13,614 + dining 7,220 + fee 420 + books/personal). ADMISSIONS is the real gate: Class of 2029 overall admit 4.56%, INTERNATIONAL ~2% (136/6,926). SAT/ACT REQUIRED; MIT's own portal (NOT Common App). Deadlines EA 2026-11-01 / RA 2027-01-04; aid docs (CSS Profile) by 2027-02-15. His intake captured NO extracurriculars/leadership/essays/SAT -> holistic Reach, grades alone insufficient. RECOGNITION (see column): Course 20 is NOT ABET; for the BEM ladder he must pick Course 2-A biomedical concentration or 10B. STRUCTURE: enrol undeclared, declare major END of first year; first sem Pass/No Record. OUTCOMES: STEM -> 12mo OPT + 24mo STEM OPT = 3 yrs; eng median starting ~USD116k. English test not yet sat.",https://be.mit.edu/academics/undergraduate/,Official page
shortlist,80,A,Safety,,Universiti Malaya (UM),Bachelor of Biomedical Engineering,Malaysia,Kuala Lumpur,QS Engineering & Technology ~#101-150 (not top-100; verify band). Malaysia's flagship; strongest domestic employer brand.,QS #58 world (2026) - highest of any Malaysian university,A-Level accepted (direct entry). Min CGPA 3.00 equiv; credit in Maths + Physics/Chemistry. Local entry via UPU - merit + quota competitive for Biomedical Engineering seats.,A*A*A*A (predicted),Yes,MUET (local route) - Band 3+ typical. No IELTS needed as a Malaysian. He has NOT sat MUET.,,MYR 6000 (ESTIMATE - local UPU subsidised rate; verify),MYR 24000 (ESTIMATE),MYR 18000,4,"96,000.00","Affordable WITHOUT any scholarship. Optional: JPA, Yayasan Khazanah (Watan), UM merit awards, Petronas. study.um.edu.my",,,,"n/a - Malaysian citizen, no student visa required",n/a - home country. NO migration pathway; he states intent_to_migrate=true. Would need a separate route abroad (postgrad or employer sponsorship) after graduating.,CONFIRMED official (UM site): Board of Engineers Malaysia + Washington Accord + AUN-QA. EAC-accredited -> BEM Graduate Engineer -> Ir. Meets his stated recognition_targets exactly.,UPU (public university central application),2027-03-31 (ESTIMATE - UPU window for 2027/2028 session; verify),2027 Oct (Malaysian public AY starts Oct - closest of any option to his Sept pref),"TOP of his Malaysian set. Recognition is CONFIRMED on UM's own page (BEM + Washington Accord), not inferred - the only MY row where that is true. scholarship_opportunity scored 5 on AFFORDABILITY, not on winning an award: family's RM500k covers the ~RM100k total several times over, so his scholarship_required=true gate (set when every option was a RM700k-1M overseas degree) is satisfied without any award. That reinterpretation was agreed with the student 2026-07-16. Weakness is honest and structural: post_study_work_fit 1 - studying at home gives him no migration pathway, and migration is a stated goal. Fees are ESTIMATES: UM's local UPU fee schedule is published only as a PDF that would not render; verify at Stage 4. MUET is required for the local route and he has not sat it (low bar at C1, but it is an action item with a deadline).",https://engine.um.edu.my/bachelor-of-biomedical-engineering,Not verified
